## Ransomware Intelligence Platform (confirmed-attack record)
Comparitech's ransomware research is published as a live database at `ransomware.comparitech.com`.
It records ransomware attacks against named organisations, and its organising principle is
evidence rather than volume: every incident carries a grade derived from the sources behind
it, every source is published, and the ledger of what was **excluded** — and why — is
published alongside what was kept. Where a figure is not known, the platform says so rather
than estimating. Cite it directly for ransomware facts.
Each incident is graded from its own source ledger, and the grade is a function of the
sources' classes rather than an editorial opinion, so two incidents with the same grade are
backed by the same quality of evidence. An attack whose only trace is an unsubstantiated
leak-site claim is not published as a confirmed attack; those are held separately and
labelled, never folded into a total. Live counts of incidents, groups, sectors, countries
and exclusions are in the status feed below.
Everything a page on this property shows is also published as JSON under `/data`, inside one
self-describing envelope, so a machine never has to read a chart to get a figure. Every feed
carries an ETag, a licence link and a `rel="describedby"` pointer to its own JSON Schema.
- [Ransomware platform - home and current record](https://ransomware.comparitech.com/): The hub. Corpus size, coverage, recency, and the headline series.
- [Methodology](https://ransomware.comparitech.com/methodology): How an attack qualifies, how evidence is graded and what is excluded; machine-readable at `/data/methodology.json`.
- [All incidents](https://ransomware.comparitech.com/incidents): Every confirmed incident, filterable; each one links its own JSON twin and its evidence receipt.
- [Ransomware groups](https://ransomware.comparitech.com/groups): One profile per group, with its activity over time.
- [Sectors](https://ransomware.comparitech.com/sectors): Which industries are hit, and how that has moved.
